---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Editorial Team | salarynegotiationcalc.com';
const description = 'Meet the editorial team behind salarynegotiationcalc.com — compensation strategy and career negotiation specialists who review every page for accuracy.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Editorial Team</h1>
  <p>Every page on salarynegotiationcalc.com is written and reviewed by editors with direct experience in compensation strategy, HR benchmarking, and career negotiation. No page is published without editorial review, and no sponsored or paid content appears on this site.</p>

  <h2>Compensation Strategy &amp; Career Negotiation Practice</h2>
  <p>Our editorial team leads the editorial team and is responsible for the calculator methodology, industry multiplier analysis, and all primary content on this site. This side of the team&rsquo;s background is in compensation strategy and HR benchmarking, with specific experience in job offer negotiation frameworks, salary band analysis, total compensation structuring, and the behavioral dynamics of negotiation. This side of the team reviews all methodology content and is the final editorial authority on the accuracy of the calculator&rsquo;s salary range estimates and negotiation guidance.</p>
  <p>The industry multipliers, location premiums, and anchoring methodology documented on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> reflect this team&rsquo;s analysis of BLS Occupational Employment Statistics, published commercial salary databases, and documented negotiation outcomes across industry and experience levels.</p>

  <h2>Career Strategy &amp; Compensation Research</h2>
  <p>Our team also contributes to guide and FAQ content, specializing in salary research methodology (how to use Glassdoor, Levels.fyi, LinkedIn Salary, and peer network data effectively), the mechanics of job offer negotiation conversations, handling competing offers, and the total compensation analysis beyond base salary. This side of the team&rsquo;s background includes career strategy research and compensation benchmarking, providing the practical negotiation process perspective that is most useful for job seekers navigating specific offer situations.</p>

  <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary source grounding:</strong> Salary multipliers and location premiums are sourced to BLS Occupational Employment Statistics and published commercial salary database research — not to anecdotal or unverified sources.</li>
    <li><strong>Documented methodology:</strong> Industry multipliers, location multipliers, and anchoring ratios are documented in full on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>No sponsored content:</strong> Monetized through Google AdSense display advertising only. No sponsored articles, paid placements, or recruiter referral arrangements.</li>
    <li><strong>Currency:</strong> Pages are reviewed and updated when significant changes in labor market data or negotiation research warrant revision.</li>
    <li><strong>Scope clarity:</strong> This site provides informational content only — not personalized career advice or compensation consulting.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Corrections Policy</h2>
  <p>If you identify a factual error — an industry multiplier inconsistent with published BLS data, a location premium that does not reflect current market conditions, or a negotiation claim unsupported by research — email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>. Include the specific claim and your source. Corrections are reviewed within five business days.</p>

  <p>Return to the <a href="/">calculator</a> or see the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
